  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with pca_n2000 (singleprofile) achieves 0.485 acc, and adding resnet50 via concat fusion yields a modest 0.527 acc (config_016), while image alone is very weak (0.208). This suggests RNA is the dominant signal and the image provides a small complementary boost. Key uncertainty: whether multiprofile (with avgpool aggregation) meaningfully improves the RNA representation beyond singleprofile. This experiment (config_002) isolates the multiprofile effect on the strongest modality by comparing directly against config_001 (same encoder, same modality, only profile setting and aggregation differ). If multiprofile substantially lifts RNA accuracy, it justifies investing remaining budget in multiprofile multimodal configs (e.g., config_018/020); if it does not, we can focus on fusion strategy (config_017) or stronger image encoders (config_022). This is the highest-information single experiment before committing to more complex multimodal-multiprofile combinations."
}

